# 🧠 What Did We Learn?

## 🔴 Vulnerability

The application directly incorporates user-controlled input into a Jinja2 template.

This allows an attacker to inject template expressions and, in this environment, access Python functionality and execute operating-system commands.

---

## 🛡️ Security Lessons

| ✅ Secure Practice                          | ❌ What Went Wrong                                  |
| :----------------------------------------- | :------------------------------------------------- |
| Treat user input strictly as data          | User input was interpreted as template code        |
| Keep user input separate from templates    | Raw input reached the template engine              |
| Validate and constrain input               | No effective protection against template injection |
| Avoid exposing dangerous objects/functions | Python functionality became reachable              |

---

